adjudication.rationale:
In handleCancelBooking.ts, the new fallback path explicitly fetches an arbitrary credential by ID from the DB when it is not found on bookingToDelete.user.credentials:

```ts
let calendarCredential = bookingToDelete.user.credentials.find((c) => c.id === credentialId);
if (!calendarCredential) {
  const foundCalendarCredential = await prisma.credential.findUnique({ where: { id: credentialId } });
  if (foundCalendarCredential) calendarCredential = foundCalendarCredential;
}
...
apiDeletes.push(calendar?.deleteEvent(uid, evt, externalCalendarId))
```

This uses the credential purely based on `credentialId` from the booking reference, with no verification that the fetched credential belongs to the booking’s organizer/user or to an allowed team/org context. That is exactly the ownership/team-membership check the finding complains is missing, and it’s a security/correctness defect introduced by this diff (previous code only used credentials attached to the booking owner).
